            "review_title": "Review at Chao Sup Linh Hoa",
            "review_text": "JSTrip_77\nSarajevo, Bosnia and Herzegovina1194 contributions\n0\nDelicious Porridge - Get there early!\nJan 2019 • Solo\nLinh Hoa is actually a chain of porridge restaurants but this is the only one I've been to. My Vietnamese friends recognize it as a very good brand. I showed up at around 9:30am one day and found that they'd pretty much run out of most of their options. So, I decided to go back the next day. Now, this might sound bad but in reality, porridge is a breakfast food (and then later, and afternoon snack). So the fact that they were out was not bad. It just meant that they make small batches thereby ensuring freshness. The morning I actually ate, they had options for chicken, pork, fish, shrimp and and I think another option. They staff make your porridge to-order so it's nice and hot when you get it. And yes, I'm often told that porridge is for \"children and old people.\" But, I didn't care. I ate it and loved it. It's hot, filling and nutritious. \n\nOh, and it's cheap! My large chicken porridge cost 15,000 dong which is about USD 0.70.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 5, 2019",
